clk: mdss-pll: keep mdss_io_util.h when the fbdev MDSS driver is used

drivers/clk/qcom/mdss/mdss-pll.h picks its I/O helper header with
"#if defined(CONFIG_DRM)": sde_io_util.h for the SDE/DRM display stack,
mdss_io_util.h otherwise. The two headers define struct dss_vreg and
struct dss_clk differently (mdss_io_util.h has load[], lp_disable_allowed,
disabled in dss_vreg; sde_io_util.h has max_rate in dss_clk).

This device uses the fbdev MDSS display driver (CONFIG_FB_MSM_MDSS), and the
msm_dss_*() helpers the PLL driver calls (msm_dss_enable_vreg(),
msm_dss_config_vreg(), msm_dss_enable_clk(), ...) are the ones built from
drivers/video/fbdev/msm/mdss_io_util.c, i.e. the mdss layout.

With CONFIG_DRM=y (enabled only to get the vgem render node) the PLL driver
was therefore compiled against the sde layout and handed arrays of the wrong
element size to the mdss helpers. The DSI PLL rail/clock handling is wrong on
every panel power cycle, so after the screen turns off it cannot be turned
on again (power button and double-tap do nothing).

Only use the sde header when DRM is enabled and the fbdev MDSS driver is not.

diff --git a/drivers/clk/qcom/mdss/mdss-pll.h b/drivers/clk/qcom/mdss/mdss-pll.h
index 5290c7cf9..4682ac6ad 100644
--- a/drivers/clk/qcom/mdss/mdss-pll.h
+++ b/drivers/clk/qcom/mdss/mdss-pll.h
@@ -12,9 +12,9 @@
 #include "../clk-regmap.h"
 #include "../clk-regmap-divider.h"
 #include "../clk-regmap-mux.h"
 
-#if defined(CONFIG_DRM)
+#if defined(CONFIG_DRM) && !defined(CONFIG_FB_MSM_MDSS)
 #include <linux/sde_io_util.h>
 #else
 #include <linux/mdss_io_util.h>
 #endif
